\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Minimum detectable SNR for each classification statement. All injections performed in a simulated A+ configuration that included aVirgo and Kagra. The top two plots both pertain to mechanism classification, and the bottom two are for g-modes and SASI. \leavevmode {\color  {red}Because there are so many different logB's we look at in this study we should have better labels for the y-axes in these figures. For example, in the last SMEE paper we used $logB_{S,N}$ and $logB_{Magrot-Neu}$. In the g-mode figure, if some waveforms have g-modes and some do not shouldn't some of the lines be positive and others negative if you plotted $logB_{gmode- nogmode}$? Same for SASI. It would be good if waveforms that are the same have the same colour in all figures. Yak switches between red, green and yellow.} }}{10}{}}
\newlabel{fig:min_snr}{{6}{10}{}{}{}}
